@inherits LayoutComponentBase

@*
    The split layout every anonymous screen shares (REQ-UI-001..004): a brand panel on the left and
    the centred form card on the right, so sign in, register, forgot and reset read as one flow.

    TR-001 is closed: this layout no longer declares `--sidebar` / `--alert-*`. TrBlazeUI 2.1.0-ci.10
    defines every one of them, so `bg-sidebar` on the brand panel now paints the REAL `--sidebar`
    (`#0f0f0f` dark) that `docs/mockups/login.html` line 106 draws, instead of the `--muted` this
    layout used to force it to, and the tick beside each benefit takes the one `--alert-success`
    declared in app.css instead of a second copy declared here.

    TR-003's `CenteredPanel` is deliberately NOT used for the right-hand half. It is a full-height
    PAGE wrapper whose panel is `max-w-sm` (24rem), `max-w-md` (28rem) or `max-w-2xl` — and this is
    not a page, it is one of two flex children of a `100vh` row, whose panel the mockup fixes at
    400px (`.authc{max-width:400px}`) and which stacks two cards with a 1rem gap. Adopting it would
    nest a second full-height wrapper and change the card's width to something the mockup does not
    draw, so `.auth-right` / `.auth-panel` stay.

    The `.auth-*` rules live in wwwroot/app.css, NOT in a co-located AuthLayout.razor.css.
    That is deliberate (REQ-NFR-015): they used to sit in the scoped-CSS bundle, which made this
    whole screen depend on one optional file — when TfLens.styles.css did not arrive, sign-in
    collapsed into an unstyled single column with no error anywhere. It reached the owner in UAT
    (2026-08-28, docs/uatissuessc/Login.png). app.css is served straight from wwwroot and does not
    go through the static-web-assets manifest. Do not move these rules back into a scoped file.
*@

<div class="auth-split">
    <aside class="auth-brand bg-sidebar" data-testid="auth-brand-panel">
        <div>
            <div class="auth-word">
                <span class="auth-mark bg-primary text-primary-foreground">
                    <LucideIcon Name="aperture" Size="24" />
                </span>
                <span class="auth-wordmark">TfLens</span>
            </div>

            <p class="auth-tagline text-muted-foreground">
                A read-only lens over TechieFlow and AI-First-Playbook telemetry
            </p>

            <ul class="auth-bullets">
                @foreach (var vBenefit in Benefits)
                {
                    <li>
                        <LucideIcon Name="check" Size="18" Class="auth-tick" />
                        <span>@vBenefit</span>
                    </li>
                }
            </ul>
        </div>

        @* REQ-UI-009, added 2026-08-29: every auth mockup puts the theme toggle here, at the foot of
           the brand panel beside the credit line. All four anonymous screens shipped without one, so a
           visitor who preferred the light palette had no way to choose it until after signing in. *@
        <div class="auth-brand-footer">
            <p class="text-xs text-muted-foreground">Free &amp; open source · identity by AppManager</p>
            <ThemeToggle TestId="theme-toggle-auth" Id="auth-theme-toggle" />
        </div>
    </aside>

    <section class="auth-right">
        <div class="auth-panel">
            @Body
        </div>
    </section>
</div>

@code {
    /// <summary>
    /// The four benefit lines shown beside the form on every anonymous screen.
    /// </summary>
    /// <remarks>
    /// The strings are the approved mockup's, verbatim (docs/TfLens-UIDesign.md, Screen: Login) — they
    /// are the product's one-line promise and are not paraphrased per screen.
    /// </remarks>
    private static readonly string[] Benefits =
    [
        "Both frameworks, one dashboard",
        "Connect any public repo",
        "Numbers you can quote",
        "Free & open source"
    ];
}
